('valenzuela_faculty', '200 Pilar Valenzuela | Chapman University Skip to main content Some of the content on this website requires JavaScript to be enabled in your web\n                  browser to function as intended. This includes, but is not limited to: navigation,\n                  video, image galleries, etc. While the website is still usable without JavaScript,\n                  it should be enabled to enjoy the full interactive experience. Dr. Pilar Valenzuela Professor World Languages and Cultures, Wilkinson College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Media Contact » Lecture/Speaker Requests » Office Location: DeMille Hall 120 B Office Hours: Mo, Tu 2:30-3:30 and by appointment Phone: (714) 997-6516 Email: valenzuela@chapman.edu Website: http://www.pilarvalenzuela.com/ Scholarly Works: Digital Commons Education: Pontifical Catholic University of Peru, Bachelor of Arts University of Oregon, Master of Arts University of Oregon, Ph.D. Biography Pilar Valenzuela earned a B.A. in Hispanic Linguistics and Literature and a Diploma\n                                    in Anthropology from the Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú, as well as an M.A.\n                                    and Ph.D. in Lin', [('Doherty, Jaime, Artidoro Tuanama and Pilar Valenzuela. 2024. Quechua de San Martín. In Enciclopedia de las lenguas del Perú en el Bicentenario, Tomo 1, pp. 29-48. Lima: Ministerio de Cultura.', 'chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://centroderecursos.cultura.pe/sites/default/files/rb/pdf/Enciclopedia%20LLII%20Bicentenario-2.pdf'), ('Valenzuela, Pilar, Alonso Vásquez and Fidel Chota. 2024. Shiwilu, Familia Kawapana, Enciclopedia de las lenguas del Perú en el Bicentenario, Tomo 1, pp. 143-164. Lima: Ministerio de Cultura.', 'chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://centroderecursos.cultura.pe/sites/default/files/rb/pdf/Enciclopedia%20LLII%20Bicentenario-2.pdf'), ('Valenzuela Bismarck, Pilar. “Difusión de rasgos andinos y elementos para una sub-área lingüística intermedia Andes-Amazonia en el norte del Perú.” In Alejandra Regúnaga, Silvia Spinelli and María Emilia Orden (comps.), IV Encuentro Internacional de Lenguas Indígenas Americanas. Libro de Actas, pp. 657-684. Santa Rosa, Argentina: Universidad Nacional de la Pampa. 2018.', 'http://www.unlpam.edu.ar/images/extension/edunlpam/Actas%20ELIA%20-%20UNLPam.pdf')])
